er the last episode of "The Next Food Network Star".', 'sentence_ids': [0, 1, 2, 3], 'score': None}, {'title': 'Rebel Eats', 'text': 'Rebel Eats is an American television pilot that aired on Food Network in 2013. The show was produced by Justin Warner.', 'sentence_ids': [0, 1], 'score': None}, {'title': 'Damaris Phillips', 'text': 'Damaris Lennon Phillips (born December 8, 1980) is an American chef and television personality. In 2013 she won the ninth season of the Food Network television series "Food Network Star". She hosted the Food Network show "Southern at Heart" for five seasons from 2013 to 2016. She currently co-hosts "The Bobby and Damaris Show" on Food Network with Bobby Flay.', 'sentence_ids': [0, 1, 2, 3], 'score': None}, {'title': 'Food Network Star Kids', 'text': 'Food Network Star Kids is an American cooking competition television series that airs on Food Network, presented by actress Tia Mowry and food critic Donal Skehan. The series is a spin-off of "Food Network Star".', 'sentence_ids': [0, 1], 'score': None}, {'title': 'Food Network Star', 'text': 'Food Network Star is a reality television series that premiered June 5, 2005. It was produced by CBS EYEtoo Productions for Seasons 1-8 and by Triage Entertainment for subsequent seasons. It airs on the Food Network in the United States. Prior to season seven, the series was known as The Next Food Network Star.', 'sentence_ids': [0, 1, 2, 3], 'score': None}, {'title': 'Justin Warner', 'text': 'Justin M. Warner (born in Hagerstown, Maryland) is an American chef. He is perhaps best known as the winner of the eighth season of the Food Network series "Food Network Star". He is the author of "The Laws of Cooking: And How to Break Them" (2015).', 'sentence_ids': [0, 1, 2], 'score': None}, {'title': 'Jaymee Sire', 'text': 'Jaymee Sire (born August 25, 1980) is a television host, sportscaster and blogger who previously worked for ESPN. She anchored SportsCenter:AM, the morning installment of the network\'s flagship show, which aired live Monday-Friday from 7am-10am ET. On July 25, 2017, it was announced that she would be the new floor reporter for Iron Chef Showdown, which will air in 4th quarter of 2017 on Food Network. She also appeared on Season 12, Episode 13 of Beat Bobby Flay, which debuted on July 13, 2017 on Food Network and as a judge on Season 13 of Food Network Star with the final four contestants. She also runs her own food blog, "E is for Eat" .', 'sentence_ids': [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 'score': None}, {'title': 'Food Network Star (season 11)', 'text': 'The eleventh season of the American reality television series Food Network Star premiered June 7, 2015 on Food Network. Food Network chefs Bobby Flay and Giada de Laurentiis returned to the series as judges, with Alton Brown not returning for undisclosed reasons. This season also continued the inclusion of "Star Salvation", a six-week webseries that featured the most recently eliminated contestant competing against the remaining previously eliminated contestants for a chance to re-enter the main "Food Network Star" competition.', 'sentence_ids': [0, 1, 2], 'score': None}, {'title': 'Will Work for Food (TV series)', 'text': 'Will Work For Food is a Food Network show starring Adam Gertler, one of three finalists of the fourth season of "The Next Food Network Star". The show premiered on Monday, January 19, 2009 at 8:30 PM EDT. According to Food Network, the series "exposes Adam to the world of little-known food jobs as he fearlessly puts his life – and mouth – on the line to try them all! Whether taking honey from three million bees, sculpting ice with a chain saw, foraging for truffles, or digging a wine cave, Adam will do anything in the name of food." The concept is somewhat similar to the Food Network program "Glutton for Punishment".', 'sentence_ids': [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 'score': None}]}) (input_keys={'candidate_passages', 'question'}): Adapter JSONAdapter failed to parse the LM response. 

